DOLLY 7
PACKAGE voxel-flyover
REQUIRES HOST runtime@0
REQUIRES HOST audio@0
REQUIRES HOST display@0
REQUIRES HOST input@0
REQUIRES HOST threads@0
REQUIRES HOST sockets@0
REQUIRES HOST gpu@0
REQUIRES HOST clipboard@0

# Voxel Flyover: an airship's flight over an endless world of blocks through a day and a night,
# drawn by Godot's Forward+ renderer on gpu@0. The world is a function its shaders compute: the
# vertex stage raises grids of boxes into ground, trees and clouds around the airship. Its
# project (demos/godot/voxel-flyover) is imported and exported here by Godot's editor, and
# voxel-flyover plays the pack with godot, which installs with it. The project installs too.
FROM /v0.1.6/Dollyfile-system 33e5bcf65ef4a634da5dbf8e291a379148e7971aa0411fe1bdaa4e0332f24b94
INSTALL /v0.1.6/demos/godot/Dollyfile-godot baadc1405822d84085538468420f096d55c4d809a1a112c100ad6076f3a1b16c
USE /v0.1.6/demos/godot/Dollyfile-godot-editor 331ba631756d21a69ab3046a333fa1cb4cedff191eb5b9ade6cac1147d23b470

REQUIRES TOOL cp
REQUIRES TOOL godot-editor
REQUIRES TOOL mkdir
REQUIRES TOOL rm
REQUIRES TOOL tar

SOURCE /v0.1.6/dist/static/godot/voxel-flyover.tar 855cb0ac566e9ce4384b6e7042a94fc7c5e2b69baebe17fc3e98af47d09fe259 /tmp/voxel-flyover.tar
SLOP CWD / tar -xf /tmp/voxel-flyover.tar
SLOP mkdir -p /usr/share/voxel-flyover
SLOP cp -r /usr/src/voxel-flyover /usr/share/voxel-flyover/project
SLOP CWD /usr/src/voxel-flyover godot-editor --headless --import
SLOP CWD /usr/src/voxel-flyover godot-editor --headless --export-pack Dolly /usr/share/voxel-flyover/voxel-flyover.pck
SLOP rm -rf /usr/src/voxel-flyover /tmp/voxel-flyover.tar

FILE /usr/bin/voxel-flyover
    #!/bin/slop
    godot --main-pack /usr/share/voxel-flyover/voxel-flyover.pck "$@"
EXPORTS TOOL voxel-flyover
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/voxel-flyover.1
    voxel-flyover [GODOT-OPTION...] [-- --autopilot SECONDS] [-- --day HOUR] [-- --scale FACTOR] [-- --plain]
    Plays Voxel Flyover on the page: an airship flies over an endless world of
    blocks, from dawn through the day into night, and lights the beacons it
    reaches. It flies itself until Enter takes the helm: arrows or WASD steer,
    climb and dive, Space is full speed, T lets the hours run, Escape lets go
    of the helm, Q quits. With --autopilot it flies by itself for that long and
    prints its frame rate, the beacons it lit and what its frame shows; --day
    starts at that hour, --scale renders the 3D view smaller and --plain leaves
    out SSAO and the volumetric fog. It draws through WebGPU (gpu@0). Its
    project is /usr/share/voxel-flyover/project: copy it to edit it with
    godot-editor.
FILE /usr/share/voxel-flyover/voxel-flyover.pck
FOLDER /usr/share/voxel-flyover/project
